<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kościuszko Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1794</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kosciuszko Uprising was a revolt led by Tadeusz Kosciuszko in 1794 against Russian and Prussian domination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-partition-of-poland">Second Partition</a>. Despite early successes, it was crushed by Russian and Prussian forces. Its defeat led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-partition-of-poland">Third Partition</a> of 1795, which ended the Commonwealth's existence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kosciuszko-uprising.jpg" alt="Kościuszko Uprising" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:BorysMapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ko%C5%9Bciuszko_uprising.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
